  "summary": "Chapter 10, Continuous solutions and normalization, receives a complete recursive reader revision. Connected opening paragraphs explain smooth approximation, Gauduchon bounds, modified comparison, uniform compactness, exponential normalization and bounded-solution regularity. Hopf near equality explicitly requires unit-integral densities with a common Lp bound and finite p>1. The concave-equation introduction declares n>=2, chi, a strict admissible-reference gap, and the derivative assumption for the gradient bound. The closing transition distinguishes scalar uniqueness from potential uniqueness. Shorter opening prose and two local pagination guards repair a detached paragraph, a split comparison statement and the positivity corollary locator. Statements, proofs and problem scopes remain unchanged. The complete final 1069-line chapter, eight inputs and 28 proofs, is read twice; complete output and dated covers are inspected. The 1758-page PDF and matching homepage description are verified live.",
